Worked for 8s

CNS — LOG 3F

Verification, Research & Decision Evaluation Fabric

Engineering Construction Specification — V1.1 FINAL

Status: FINAL / CHECKED / FREEZE
Position: 3F sits between CNS cognition/work and final decision authority.

> 3B thinks. 3C organizes. 3D supplies resources. 3E remembers. 3F researches, verifies, challenges and evaluates decision readiness. CNS decides.



I rebuilt 3F rather than simply patching the previous version. The previous ~85–90% is retained, but the architecture is now explicitly opportunity-centric, consequence-scaled and anti-paralysis.


---

0. THE PURPOSE OF 3F

3F exists because CNS cannot simply:

> “Think something → believe it → act.”



Nor should CNS become:

> “Nothing is certain → therefore never act.”



3F is the system that determines:

> What do we actually know? What might be true? What evidence supports it? What contradicts it? How robust is it? What remains unknown? How much investigation is justified? And is the evidence sufficient for the intended decision?



The fundamental distinction is:

3B → THINK
3F → RESEARCH + VERIFY + CHALLENGE + EVALUATE
CNS → DECIDE

3F therefore does not own the final decision.

It produces a trustworthy decision-evaluation state for CNS.


---

1. THE CHARACTER 3F MUST GIVE CNS

3F must preserve the character established in Log 1.

CNS is intended to be:

aggressive in opportunity pursuit

disciplined in execution

extremely sensitive to unusual signals

fast when speed matters

skeptical when evidence is weak

capable of deep investigation

capable of acting under uncertainty

resistant to false confidence

resistant to paralysis

capable of finding asymmetric opportunities

capable of rejecting bad opportunities quickly

capable of investigating promising unknowns cheaply

capable of learning from both success and failure.


Therefore:

> 3F is not a conservative gatekeeper.



It is an intelligence amplifier and truth-seeking mechanism.

Its job is not to reduce the number of actions.

Its job is to improve the quality of the actions CNS chooses.


---

2. 3F BOUNDARY

3F owns:

Research
Verification
Evidence
Contradiction analysis
Adversarial challenge
Statistical validation
Robustness testing
Experiment evaluation
Opportunity evaluation
Asymmetry analysis
Confidence/calibration
Decision-readiness evaluation
Research stopping
Evidence sufficiency
Research reproducibility
Post-decision evaluation

3F does not own:

Final CNS authority
Work decomposition
Agent spawning
Resource lifecycle
Memory ownership
Model selection
Trading execution
Portfolio authority
Risk authority
User authority

Those remain with the appropriate layers.


