63. ACCEPTANCE TESTS

3F must pass at minimum:

VER-001

Can represent a claim with provenance.

VER-002

Can represent supporting and contradicting evidence.

VER-003

Can detect evidence from the same underlying source.

VER-004

Can preserve temporal validity.

VER-005

Can distinguish research from verification.

VER-006

Can perform deterministic fact checks.

VER-007

Can perform independent challenge.

VER-008

Can preserve minority/dissent evidence.

VER-009

Can calculate/track uncertainty.

VER-010

Can evaluate calibration.

VER-011

Can evaluate opportunity rather than only claims.

VER-012

Can calculate/represent upside and downside.

VER-013

Can evaluate asymmetry.

VER-014

Can calculate/estimate VOI.

VER-015

Can choose proportionate verification effort.

VER-016

Can avoid unnecessary research.

VER-017

Can identify when deeper research is justified.

VER-018

Can represent novel opportunities without automatically rejecting them.

VER-019

Can classify early opportunities.

VER-020

Can distinguish readiness from recommendation.

VER-021

Can evaluate ACT vs WAIT vs RESEARCH vs TEST.

VER-022

Can create reproducible experiments.

VER-023

Can enforce baseline comparison.

VER-024

Can detect look-ahead leakage.

VER-025

Can detect survivorship bias.

VER-026

Can perform OOS testing.

VER-027

Can perform walk-forward evaluation.

VER-028

Can perform historical replay.

VER-029

Can perform simulation.

VER-030

Can evaluate paper-trading evidence.

VER-031

Can perform robustness testing.

VER-032

Can perform ablation.

VER-033

Can distinguish mechanistic from empirical support.

VER-034

Can preserve experiment configuration and provenance.

VER-035

Can detect failed research.

VER-036

Can invalidate contaminated conclusions.

VER-037

Can compare champion and candidate.

VER-038

Can evaluate expected vs actual outcomes.

VER-039

Can attribute errors to the correct subsystem.

VER-040

Can produce durable research ledger records.

VER-041

Can feed validated lessons into 3E.

VER-042

Can provide evidence/uncertainty to 3B.

VER-043

Can request work through 3C without taking orchestration ownership.

VER-044

Can use qualified resources from 3D.

VER-045

Cannot bypass CNS decision authority.

VER-046

Cannot directly override risk/execution controls.

VER-047

Cannot treat statistical success as proof.

VER-048

Cannot treat uncertainty as automatic rejection.

VER-049

Cannot allow endless research without stopping conditions.

VER-050

Can preserve a complete replayable research chain.


---

64. PERFORMANCE MEASURES

3F itself must be measured.

Important metrics:

verification accuracy
false acceptance
false rejection
contradiction detection rate
research resolution rate
time-to-resolution
research cost
VOI efficiency
reproducibility rate
calibration
OOS degradation
robustness
decision-readiness accuracy
novel opportunity discovery
opportunity survival rate
unnecessary research rate
research duplication
post-decision attribution accuracy

A verification system that is “safe” but rejects every opportunity is not successful.

A system that approves everything is also not successful.


---

65. 3F SUCCESS CRITERION

The real question is not:

> “Does 3F reject bad ideas?”



It is:

> Does 3F improve CNS's ability to distinguish valuable opportunities from false opportunities while using the minimum sufficient research required by the consequence and uncertainty?



That is the correct metric.


---

66. EXPLICIT NON-ASSUMPTIONS

3F does not assume:

more evidence = better evidence
more agents = better verification
more research = better decisions
more data = better result
backtest = proof
paper trading = live equivalence
statistical significance = economic significance
high confidence = correctness
LLM reasoning = verification
consensus = truth
majority vote = correctness
historical precedent = future guarantee
novel = bad
uncertain = reject
complex = intelligent
expensive = better
independent-looking sources = independent evidence
one model = ground truth

These are all explicitly rejected.


---

