V1.1: corrected through:

opportunity evaluation
asymmetry
VOI
consequence-scaled verification
early opportunity state
cheap experiments
action-mode readiness
anti-paralysis rule

PASS.


---

Attack 2 — Could 3F become another CNS brain?

No.

3F evaluates.

3B reasons.

CNS decides.

PASS.


---

Attack 3 — Could 3F become a giant research bureaucracy?

Controlled through:

VOI
minimum sufficient verification
research priority
stopping rules
reuse
consequence scaling

PASS.


---

Attack 4 — Could 3F miss extraordinary new opportunities?

V1.0 had that weakness.

V1.1 explicitly supports:

novel opportunity
early opportunity
mechanism search
asymmetry
cheap experimentation
paper/simulation/small exposure

PASS.


